low.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 9/9 and cash conversion of 1.52x.","ROE of 22% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 13pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.6x net debt to EBITDA ($416.7M of cash against $1.7B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.8x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 6.1, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.66).","Working capital ties up about 140 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.1% over 3 years, 9.0% over 5 years and 2.1% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 10% of profits supports about 1.6% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 61.5% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.96, a backlog worth 81% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 11%.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (6.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.8%), and institutions hold 98%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (31 sales, net $49.7M sold).","It returns 2.1% a year to shareholders (2.1% in buybacks).","The share count has grown 1.3% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 7,600 employees, each generates about $604K of revenue, 1.7x the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 2.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $44K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.5M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":48,"head":"Avoid: priced 260% above its fair value of $46.01.","pros":["Revenue grew 9.0%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 9/9","Altman Z in the safe zone","10 analysts' mean target $252 (+52%)","12-1 month momentum +93%"],"cons":["Trades 260% above fair value of $46.01","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 41.4x vs sector 22.1x","EV/EBITDA 24.2x vs sector 12.9x","P/FCF 67.4x vs sector 21.8x"],"flags":["Priced 260% above its fair value of $46.01"],"need":[],"buy_below":39.11,"vc":{"base":46.01,"base_src":"dcf","bear":26.97,"bull":77.58,"alt_median":25.29,"n_alt":1,"gap":0.8192,"dispersion":0.2906,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 82% above the other models' median ($25.29)"]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"mc_quantiles":[16.24,21.72,26.97,29.89,32.41,35.17,37.71,39.45,41.34,44.19,46.63,48.74,51.3,54.28,57.38,60.4,64.46,69.64,77.58,86.73,112.05],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.762,"discount_rate":0.128,"terminal_growth":0.004,"exit_multiple":0.106},"ticker":"ATI","date":"2026-11-20"}